Fix SIGSEGV when clicking the GUI background/wallpaper with no windows open

GUIgetcurrentinput() (gui/guikeys.c) computed "GUIwinptr - 1" as an
unsigned value even when GUIwinptr was 0, so GUIwinorder[0xFFFFFFFF]
was read and whatever globals neighbour GUIwinorder in BSS got
dispatched through the per-window key switch. Depending on that
garbage this segfaults, e.g. clicking the interface wallpaper with
no window open. The same code was harmless as 32-bit assembly, which
is why this only surfaced in the C11/64-bit ports.

Guard the window-key dispatch with GUIwinptr != 0: with no window
open there is nothing to dispatch to. ESC with no windows open still
quits to the game, and key handling with windows open is unchanged.
diff --git a/gui/guikeys.c b/gui/guikeys.c
index a45debae..5f0ed8df 100644
--- a/gui/guikeys.c
+++ b/gui/guikeys.c
@@ -1640,7 +1640,7 @@ done:
         if (al == 27 && GUIwinptr == 0) {
             if (romloadskip == 0)
                 GUIQuit = 2;
-        } else {
+        } else if (GUIwinptr != 0) {
             u4 const eax = GUIwinptr - 1;
             u4 const ebx = GUIwinorder[eax];
             if (al == 27 && (ebx != 13 || CheatWinMode <= 1)) { // Close window
